1
00:01:00,125 --> 00:01:01,208
Honey, help me!

2
00:01:07,625 --> 00:01:08,625
Lin Zai!

3
00:01:49,541 --> 00:01:50,541
Brother!

4
00:01:50,791 --> 00:01:51,375
Help me!

5
00:01:51,708 --> 00:01:52,250
Lin Zai!

6
00:01:52,708 --> 00:01:53,208
It's too late!

7
00:01:53,458 --> 00:01:53,958
This way!

8
00:01:54,291 --> 00:01:54,708
Hurry!

9
00:01:55,041 --> 00:01:56,041
Go!

10
00:02:11,875 --> 00:02:13,000
Hurry up, Lin Zai!

11
00:02:15,583 --> 00:02:16,583
This way!

12
00:02:16,666 --> 00:02:17,666
This way!

13
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:20,000
Over here!

14
00:02:20,416 --> 00:02:21,125
Move!

15
00:02:21,291 --> 00:02:22,291
Move!

16
00:02:24,291 --> 00:02:25,416
Brother, it won't open!

17
00:02:32,166 --> 00:02:32,625
Brother!

18
00:02:32,626 --> 00:02:33,958
The door's open! Hurry!

19
00:02:56,166 --> 00:02:57,166
Kid.

20
00:02:57,875 --> 00:02:59,583
It's not safe for us here anymore.

21
00:03:00,333 --> 00:03:01,333
We need to hurry

22
00:03:01,333 --> 00:03:02,333
and find a new way out.

23
00:03:04,583 --> 00:03:05,583
I just

24
00:03:05,666 --> 00:03:07,291
saw the floor plan in the hallway.

25
00:03:08,375 --> 00:03:09,666
I remember where the exit is.

26
00:03:10,791 --> 00:03:11,791
Brother.

27
00:03:12,125 --> 00:03:13,125
Don't worry.

28
00:03:13,458 --> 00:03:14,898
I'll definitely get you out of here.

29
00:03:16,375 --> 00:03:17,535
If my little brother says so,

30
00:03:17,833 --> 00:03:18,833
then it's a sure thing.

31
00:03:19,416 --> 00:03:20,416
Let's go.

32
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:29,000
Lin Zai!

33
00:03:34,750 --> 00:03:35,750
Brother!

34
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:37,750
Get out of here!

35
00:03:37,958 --> 00:03:39,583
You have to survive.

36
00:03:41,541 --> 00:03:42,541
Go!

37
00:03:42,833 --> 00:03:45,500
Leave me!

38
00:03:54,541 --> 00:03:55,833
Brother!

39
00:03:58,708 --> 00:03:59,708
You

40
00:03:59,709 --> 00:04:00,874
must

41
00:04:00,875 --> 00:04:02,458
live.

42
00:05:15,375 --> 00:05:16,416
My name is Lin Zai.

43
00:05:17,750 --> 00:05:18,791
Twenty-two days ago,

44
00:05:19,458 --> 00:05:20,833
the zombie outbreak suddenly hit,

45
00:05:22,125 --> 00:05:23,166
destroying my life

46
00:05:24,208 --> 00:05:25,250
and taking away my family.

47
00:05:27,375 --> 00:05:28,416
Just now,

48
00:05:28,875 --> 00:05:30,000
I lost my brother too.

49
00:05:31,833 --> 00:05:32,833
And now,

50
00:05:32,916 --> 00:05:33,916
I've been bitten as well.

51
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:36,041
It's all over.

52
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:39,000
They say

53
00:05:39,625 --> 00:05:42,166
you only have a few hours
of sanity left after being bitten.

54
00:05:44,208 --> 00:05:45,728
I didn't know it would hurt this much.

55
00:05:45,958 --> 00:05:47,038
That it would be this cold.

56
00:05:48,083 --> 00:05:49,708
I'll slowly forget who I am.

57
00:05:52,125 --> 00:05:53,166
I guess.

58
00:05:54,208 --> 00:05:55,250
I'm on my way there.

59
00:06:52,708 --> 00:06:53,750
Honey, are you okay?

60
00:06:54,375 --> 00:06:55,375
I'm fine.

61
00:06:55,376 --> 00:06:56,707
Your lips are pale.

62
00:06:56,708 --> 00:06:57,708
I'm fine.

63
00:06:57,958 --> 00:06:58,999
Why are you sweating so much?

64
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:00,000
I'm fine.

65
00:07:08,333 --> 00:07:08,916
Please!

66
00:07:09,208 --> 00:07:10,208
Please don't kill me!

67
00:07:10,416 --> 00:07:11,333
Please don't kill me!

68
00:07:11,333 --> 00:07:11,875
Please!

69
00:07:12,125 --> 00:07:12,875
Please don't kill him!

70
00:07:12,875 --> 00:07:13,250
Please!

71
00:07:13,333 --> 00:07:13,708
Please!

72
00:07:13,750 --> 00:07:14,750
Please!

73
00:07:19,333 --> 00:07:20,333
Honey!

74
00:07:20,833 --> 00:07:21,625
No immune subjects found.

75
00:07:21,625 --> 00:07:22,000
Honey!

76
00:07:22,291 --> 00:07:23,416
Keep searching.

77
00:07:38,666 --> 00:07:39,875
I didn't turn into a zombie.

78
00:07:44,244 --> 00:07:45,392
[TN: The character for "praying"]

79
00:07:45,416 --> 00:07:47,166
You have to survive.

80
00:07:53,666 --> 00:07:54,666
Brother,

81
00:07:55,250 --> 00:07:56,875
I promise I will survive.

82
00:07:57,708 --> 00:07:59,108
Even if it's just for one more day.

83
00:09:40,500 --> 00:09:44,500
"The Last Oath"

84
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:49,500
(Episode 1: Infection)

85
00:09:53,129 --> 00:09:56,376
(Six months later)

86
00:10:08,416 --> 00:10:10,250
Lin Zai, come here for a sec!

87
00:10:10,375 --> 00:10:11,791
Coming!

88
00:10:17,083 --> 00:10:18,083
What's up, Brother Li?

89
00:10:18,541 --> 00:10:20,625
I changed the bulb, but
it's still not turning on.

90
00:10:20,958 --> 00:10:21,708
Let me take a look.

91
00:10:21,709 --> 00:10:22,749
You need to fix it quick.

92
00:10:22,750 --> 00:10:24,040
Zombies got in last night.

93
00:10:24,041 --> 00:10:24,458
What?

94
00:10:24,458 --> 00:10:25,166
Don't panic.

95
00:10:25,167 --> 00:10:26,500
Sister Chen took care of it.

96
00:10:26,916 --> 00:10:27,916
Sister Chen is the best.

97
00:10:27,916 --> 00:10:28,916
Here, hand it to me.

98
00:10:29,083 --> 00:10:30,083
Careful now.

99
00:10:37,458 --> 00:10:38,458
Here, try it.

100
00:10:40,416 --> 00:10:41,416
Awesome.

101
00:10:43,291 --> 00:10:43,916
Let's go.

102
00:10:43,916 --> 00:10:44,666
Let's go grab some food.

103
00:10:44,791 --> 00:10:45,291
Okay.

104
00:10:45,583 --> 00:10:47,040
College kids really know their stuff.

105
00:10:47,041 --> 00:10:48,332
All I can do is change a bulb

106
00:10:48,333 --> 00:10:49,333
or fix a faucet.

107
00:10:49,416 --> 00:10:50,499
For delicate work like this,

108
00:10:50,500 --> 00:10:51,916
we have to rely on you.

109
00:10:52,708 --> 00:10:53,291
Brother Li,

110
00:10:53,291 --> 00:10:53,583
Yeah?

111
00:10:53,584 --> 00:10:55,041
you're the one with super strength.

112
00:10:55,250 --> 00:10:57,890
You carried me up five flights
of stairs without breaking a sweat.

113
00:10:57,916 --> 00:10:58,916
When it counts,

114
00:10:59,125 --> 00:11:01,040
you're way more useful than I am.

115
00:11:01,041 --> 00:11:02,082
Listen here, you brat.

116
00:11:02,083 --> 00:11:03,249
Are you indirectly calling me

117
00:11:03,250 --> 00:11:04,749
all brawn and no brains?

118
00:11:04,750 --> 00:11:05,083
No, no, not at all.

119
00:11:05,083 --> 00:11:05,916
Next time we haul supplies,

120
00:11:05,917 --> 00:11:07,124
you're carrying double the load.

121
00:11:07,125 --> 00:11:08,351
Otherwise, don't bother coming back.

122
00:11:08,375 --> 00:11:09,375
And no dinner for you.

123
00:11:09,916 --> 00:11:11,415
I was just about to go in and get you two.

124
00:11:11,416 --> 00:11:12,125
Time to eat!

125
00:11:12,125 --> 00:11:13,125
Grandma Qiu, let me help.

126
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:15,541
Oh, my.

127
00:11:15,542 --> 00:11:16,790
People need to eat.

128
00:11:16,791 --> 00:11:18,726
You need a full stomach
to have the energy to work.

129
00:11:18,750 --> 00:11:19,750
Today,

130
00:11:19,916 --> 00:11:22,208
we have the sparrow
meat you've been craving.

131
00:11:25,375 --> 00:11:27,495
Hold your horses. We'll eat
when Xiao Chen gets here.

132
00:11:29,958 --> 00:11:30,958
Where is Xiao Chen?

133
00:11:31,125 --> 00:11:32,125
Xiao Chen?

134
00:11:32,541 --> 00:11:34,125
She should be in the backyard.

135
00:11:34,375 --> 00:11:35,375
I'll go get her.

136
00:11:36,291 --> 00:11:37,291
Okay.

137
00:11:49,375 --> 00:11:50,791
Sister Chen, food's ready!

138
00:12:08,625 --> 00:12:11,040
Good thing you suggested
adding more defenses yesterday.

139
00:12:11,041 --> 00:12:13,416
Otherwise, we would've
been toast last night.

140
00:12:14,916 --> 00:12:15,833
As long as it works.

141
00:12:15,834 --> 00:12:17,354
But we still can't let our guard down.

142
00:12:18,666 --> 00:12:19,666
Oh, come on.

143
00:12:20,166 --> 00:12:21,166
It's fine.

144
00:12:21,625 --> 00:12:22,625
Don't worry.

145
00:12:22,833 --> 00:12:24,041
Our camp is well hidden.

146
00:12:24,375 --> 00:12:25,695
A few stray zombies now and then?

147
00:12:25,916 --> 00:12:28,291
I can handle them with my eyes closed.

148
00:12:29,625 --> 00:12:30,785
You're a badass, Sister Chen.

149
00:12:30,916 --> 00:12:32,624
I'm going to double-check the other traps.

150
00:12:32,625 --> 00:12:33,999
You go ahead and eat.

151
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:35,333
Alright, be careful.

152
00:13:09,916 --> 00:13:10,916
Brother.

153
00:13:12,375 --> 00:13:15,208
You must be watching over me
from heaven, keeping me from turning.

154
00:13:16,041 --> 00:13:17,250
Until my time comes,

155
00:13:17,916 --> 00:13:19,416
I promise I'll survive.

156
00:14:19,166 --> 00:14:20,166
Go!

157
00:14:20,458 --> 00:14:21,500
Leave me!

158
00:14:26,791 --> 00:14:27,250
Go!

159
00:14:27,541 --> 00:14:28,541
Leave me!

160
00:14:49,500 --> 00:14:50,500
Don't touch him!

161
00:14:51,458 --> 00:14:52,458
What are you doing?

162
00:14:52,541 --> 00:14:53,750
What if he's a zombie?

163
00:15:11,708 --> 00:15:12,868
Looks like he's not infected.

164
00:15:16,500 --> 00:15:19,291
These are just fall and scrape wounds.

165
00:15:21,666 --> 00:15:23,375
Looks like he fell from somewhere.

166
00:15:23,833 --> 00:15:25,993
Probably has some internal
injuries and fractures too.

167
00:15:26,041 --> 00:15:27,458
To make it all the way to our camp,

168
00:15:28,166 --> 00:15:29,207
he must have run into

169
00:15:29,208 --> 00:15:30,448
a lot of zombies along the way.

170
00:15:33,458 --> 00:15:34,625
Can he be saved?

171
00:15:35,166 --> 00:15:35,791
Hard to say.

172
00:15:35,792 --> 00:15:37,208
But we'd better stay out of this.

173
00:15:38,208 --> 00:15:39,958
We're already low on supplies.

174
00:15:40,750 --> 00:15:41,791
And looking at his gear,

175
00:15:42,125 --> 00:15:44,083
he might even be a looter.

176
00:15:44,750 --> 00:15:46,350
We have to prioritize the camp's safety.

177
00:15:56,875 --> 00:15:57,375
Buddy,

178
00:15:57,625 --> 00:15:58,625
I'm sorry.

179
00:15:58,708 --> 00:16:00,208
We'd love to help,

180
00:16:00,500 --> 00:16:01,500
but our hands are tied.

181
00:16:02,375 --> 00:16:03,375
Sorry about this.

182
00:16:16,833 --> 00:16:17,833
Whoa.

183
00:16:18,083 --> 00:16:19,083
Bandages,

184
00:16:20,875 --> 00:16:22,250
a huge coil of climbing rope,

185
00:16:25,666 --> 00:16:26,708
and a small flashlight.

186
00:16:28,416 --> 00:16:29,791
This guy's no joke.

187
00:16:33,583 --> 00:16:34,583
Food,

188
00:16:34,625 --> 00:16:35,625
tools.

189
00:16:36,750 --> 00:16:38,375
Everything our camp needs.

190
00:16:38,958 --> 00:16:39,999
Aside from looters,

191
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:40,833
I doubt anyone would

192
00:16:40,834 --> 00:16:42,332
carry such a complete set of gear

193
00:16:42,333 --> 00:16:43,613
while wandering around out here.

194
00:16:51,375 --> 00:16:52,708
It is pretty comprehensive.

195
00:16:53,750 --> 00:16:55,540
But in times like these,

196
00:16:55,541 --> 00:16:57,375
it's better to be safe than sorry.

197
00:16:58,083 --> 00:16:59,249
After all, this camp of ours

198
00:16:59,250 --> 00:17:00,915
took a lot of effort

199
00:17:00,916 --> 00:17:02,036
to build from the ground up.

200
00:17:02,750 --> 00:17:03,375
Yeah.

201
00:17:03,376 --> 00:17:04,541
You have a point.

202
00:17:05,166 --> 00:17:06,416
No matter the era,

203
00:17:06,875 --> 00:17:08,958
humanity's greatest enemy is always itself.

204
00:17:09,083 --> 00:17:11,458
Humanity's greatest enemy is always itself.

205
00:17:18,208 --> 00:17:19,125
All right, all right.

206
00:17:19,126 --> 00:17:20,582
Stop dwelling on it.

207
00:17:20,583 --> 00:17:22,083
Even in peacetime,

208
00:17:22,208 --> 00:17:23,874
if someone just collapsed on the street,

209
00:17:23,875 --> 00:17:25,125
people would hesitate to help.

210
00:17:25,416 --> 00:17:26,625
Let alone nowadays.

211
00:17:26,958 --> 00:17:28,290
Captain Chen made the right call.

212
00:17:28,291 --> 00:17:29,971
And you weren't wrong for wanting to help.

213
00:17:31,041 --> 00:17:31,750
I know.

214
00:17:32,041 --> 00:17:33,041
I just...

215
00:17:34,208 --> 00:17:35,041
Never mind.

216
00:17:35,041 --> 00:17:36,041
Let's drop it.

217
00:17:36,875 --> 00:17:37,833
What goodies did you find?

218
00:17:37,833 --> 00:17:38,500
Let me see.

219
00:17:38,500 --> 00:17:39,500
Hey.

220
00:17:39,541 --> 00:17:40,583
This is for kids.

221
00:17:41,041 --> 00:17:42,249
It's a bit too childish.

222
00:17:42,250 --> 00:17:43,374
It's perfect for someone like you,

223
00:17:43,375 --> 00:17:44,540
a young college guy.

224
00:17:44,541 --> 00:17:45,541
A gift from your big bro.

225
00:17:48,125 --> 00:17:49,625
Even a college guy finds it childish.

226
00:17:51,875 --> 00:17:52,875
Then...

227
00:17:52,958 --> 00:17:53,375
Hey.

228
00:17:53,875 --> 00:17:54,208
How about this?

229
00:17:54,375 --> 00:17:55,375
This one's stylish.

230
00:18:00,875 --> 00:18:02,041
Thanks, Brother Li.

231
00:18:02,875 --> 00:18:03,915
When I get the game console fixed,

232
00:18:03,916 --> 00:18:04,916
I'll let you have the first go.

233
00:18:04,917 --> 00:18:06,291
That's more like it.

234
00:20:28,375 --> 00:20:30,250
You'd better not be a Marauder.

235
00:20:30,958 --> 00:20:33,000
Otherwise, my good deed will backfire.

236
00:21:22,458 --> 00:21:22,958
Hey.

237
00:21:22,958 --> 00:21:23,541
How are you holding up?

238
00:21:23,875 --> 00:21:24,875
Hang in there.

239
00:21:32,125 --> 00:21:32,625
Hey.

240
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:33,541
Wake up.

241
00:21:33,791 --> 00:21:34,541
Wake up.

242
00:21:34,541 --> 00:21:35,541
Hey.

243
00:21:38,083 --> 00:21:38,708
Hey!

244
00:21:38,708 --> 00:21:39,708
Don't die on me.

245
00:21:39,833 --> 00:21:41,553
I went through hell to carry you back here.

246
00:21:42,000 --> 00:21:43,458
Don't let all my effort go to waste.

247
00:21:43,875 --> 00:21:44,250
Hey.

248
00:21:44,750 --> 00:21:45,750
Wake up.
